> That's what I ended up doing. I didn't feel like trying to fix the
> problem encountered by the OP, after the documented fix didn't work. I
> tried the QT and the Carbon versions, but neither of them appealed to
> me. So then I decided to give nethack.alt.org a try. Creating an
> account was quick and easy, and it took no time at all to figure out
> how to edit the defaults file, so I just pasted in the contents of my
> local one. After that, playing nethack is exactly like it was playing
> it on my local system, except that the game is slightly less responsive
> due to everything going over the network. Which I think is actually
> good, because in the long run it may prevent a few YASDs. :-)

Other advantages:
- bones files from a myriad of other players, without having to install
  hearse.
- you can follow along on the IRC #nethack channel on freenode, where a bot
  announces all the deaths that occur.  The bot (Rodney) may also be
  queried for useful information, as can the denizens of the channel.
- the server will keep track of some statistics for you (go to
  http://alt.org/nethack)
- some nice patches such as sortloot and dumplog are already installed for
  you.
- you can watch other players' games, and even send them messages as they
  play.

